{"answer": "A", "estimate": 36.5, "mechanism": "B", "confidence": 98, "reasoning": "Go maps never shrink automatically. Neither delete() nor clear() frees allocated bucket arrays; they only mark/clear slots in-place. Because the 1M-entry map grew to 2^18 buckets (144 bytes each, ~36 MB), the live bucket array remains retained on the heap even after all elements are removed."}
